<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><meta name="description" content="The 2007 Principia Evolution: a Danish aluminium racer with shaped tubes, a WEAVE carbon fork and Shimano Dura-Ace components."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="og:title" content="The 2007 Principia Evolution · The Evolution of Bikes"/><meta property="og:description" content="A Danish aluminium racer shaped by Principia’s stiffness-to-weight principle."/><meta property="og:image" content={heroSocial}/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><title>The 2007 Principia Evolution · The Evolution of Bikes</title><link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}/styles/global.css`}/></head><body><EnglishHeader current="bikes" danishPath="/cykler/principia-evolution/"/>
<main class="atala-page">
<header class="quick-hero"><p class="section-label">In the collection · Denmark · 2007</p><h1>Principia<br/><em>Evolution</em></h1><p>A Danish aluminium racer built around large shaped tubes and Principia’s original measure of performance: as much stiffness as possible for as little weight as possible.</p></header>
<figure class="quick-pass"><OptimizedImage src={hero} alt="Bronze 2007 Principia Evolution seen from the drive side" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>The aluminium frame is paired with a carbon fork and Shimano components. Photo: The Evolution of Bikes.</figcaption></figure>
<section class="atala-facts"><div><strong>2007</strong><span>Stated year</span></div><div><strong>Aluminium</strong><span>Shaped, welded tubes</span></div><div><strong>Dura-Ace</strong><span>Brakes and gear parts</span></div><div><strong>WEAVE</strong><span>Carbon fork</span></div></section>
<section class="atala-opening"><p class="section-label">Large tubes, clear purpose</p><p>The tubing dominates the bicycle. Around the head tube and bottom bracket the profiles grow large and shaped to resist twisting under hard pedalling and cornering. Principia made stiffness in relation to weight an operating principle: STW, stiffness to weight.</p></section>
<section class="atala-story"><div><p class="section-label">Aalborg, 1990</p><h2>Three triathletes began building</h2></div><div><p>Principia began in Aalborg in 1990. Three young triathletes could not afford the American aluminium frames they wanted, so they began filing, fitting and welding their own tubes in a basement on Himmerlandsgade.</p><p>Principia worked early with 7020 aluminium. The label on this Evolution, however, says “Principia Magnum aluminium tubing”. Without a contemporary model catalogue, the two descriptions should not automatically be treated as identical.</p><p>The large tubes became a visual signature. Their size also had a practical purpose: moving material farther from the tube’s centre increased resistance to bending and twisting.</p></div></section>
<section class="atala-details"><figure><OptimizedImage src={downTube} alt="Large shaped down tube of the Principia Evolution"/><figcaption>The broad down tube carries loads between the head tube and bottom-bracket area.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={tubing} alt="Label for Principia Magnum aluminium tubing"/><figcaption>The label describes tapered, CNC-machined and TIG-welded Principia Magnum tubing.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={denmark} alt="Principia of Denmark lettering on the seat tube"/><figcaption>The label refers to Danish design but does not by itself document the place of manufacture.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="atala-components"><div><p class="section-label">The 2007 bicycle</p><h2>Aluminium with carbon at the front</h2></div><div><p>The Evolution combines its aluminium frame with a WEAVE C24T monocoque carbon fork, a characteristic material mix for good road bicycles of the 2000s.</p><p>Dura-Ace markings are visible on the brakes and rear derailleur. The crankset is marked Shimano Ultegra. It is therefore more accurate to call this a build with Dura-Ace parts than a complete matching Dura-Ace groupset.</p><p>Rim brakes and external cables keep the mechanics visible. The bicycle sits just before electronic shifting, hidden cables and disc brakes changed the modern road racer’s appearance.</p></div></section>
<section class="atala-details"><figure><OptimizedImage src={frontBrake} alt="Shimano Dura-Ace front brake on the Principia Evolution"/><figcaption>The Dura-Ace rim brake acts directly on the aluminium braking surface.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={fork} alt="WEAVE C24T monocoque carbon fork label"/><figcaption>The fork is marked WEAVE C24T full monocoque carbon.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={cockpit} alt="Handlebar, stem and head tube of the Principia Evolution"/><figcaption>A separate stem and visible cables leave the front easy to read and adjust.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="atala-story"><div><p class="section-label">From Aalborg to export</p><h2>The frames went racing</h2></div><div><p>Principia grew quickly during the 1990s, helped especially by the German market. It supplied Team Chicky World, Team Acceptcard, Team Fakta and Britain’s Linda McCartney Racing Team.</p><p>On a Principia, Australian David McKenzie won stage 7 of the 2000 Giro d’Italia after spending 164 kilometres alone at the front. A small Danish frame maker had reached international professional racing.</p><p>After several changes of ownership, Principia became part of HF Christiansen in 2006. This bicycle is dated to 2007 and therefore stands close to that transition.</p></div></section>
<section class="atala-details"><figure><OptimizedImage src={rearBrake} alt="Brake bridge and rear brake on the Principia Evolution"/><figcaption>Shaped tubes and a substantial brake bridge define the rear end.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={drivetrain} alt="Dura-Ace rear derailleur and Ultegra crankset on the Principia Evolution"/><figcaption>The Dura-Ace rear derailleur is paired with an Ultegra crankset.</figcaption></figure><figure><OptimizedImage src={evolution} alt="Evolution model lettering on the rear triangle"/><figcaption>The Evolution model name runs discreetly along the rear triangle.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="koga-specs"><div><p class="section-label">The bicycle</p><h2>Brief specification</h2></div><dl><div><dt>Maker</dt><dd>Principia</dd></div><div><dt>Model</dt><dd>Evolution</dd></div><div><dt>Year</dt><dd>2007, stated</dd></div><div><dt>Frame</dt><dd>Principia Magnum aluminium tubing</dd></div><div><dt>Fork</dt><dd>WEAVE C24T monocoque carbon</dd></div><div><dt>Gears and brakes</dt><dd>Shimano Dura-Ace parts</dd></div><div><dt>Crankset</dt><dd>Shimano Ultegra</dd></div><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>In the collection</dd></div></dl></section>
<section class="atala-story period-sources"><div><p class="section-label">Sources</p><h2>Basis</h2></div><div><p><a href="https://principiabikes.com/about/history">Principia: Our history</a> · the bicycle, its labels and information supplied by its owner.</p><p>The year is supplied by the owner. Components are identified from visible markings. The maker’s history is a retrospective company account used for the broad outline of the marque.</p></div></section>
<section class="atala-closing"><p>The Evolution shows how far Principia’s original idea could be developed. Large welded aluminium tubes remain the starting point, while a carbon fork and 2000s components place it far from the first basement-built triathlon frames.</p><div class="bike-bottom-nav"><a href={`${base}/en/bikes/`}>← Back to bicycles</a><a href={`${base}/en/periods/2000-2009/`}>View the period →</a></div></section>
</main><EnglishFooter/></body></html>
